## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates ability to design private, language-aware ML inference at scale with strict data locality and per-tenant isolation. Tests routing logic, canary deployment strategies, and cross-language drift handling.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model vs. per-language endpoints
- PrivateLink data residency and IAM isolation
- Canary rollouts and per-language versioning
- Model Registry + Pipelines for safe promotions
- Tenant-scoped storage and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Language route resolver
function routeEndpoint(lang) {
  const map = {
    en: 'ep-en',
    fr: 'ep-fr',
    de: 'ep-de'
  };
  return map[lang] || 'ep-default';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design secure, scalable multi-tenant inference with cross-account PrivateLink, model registry usage, and drift-aware rollouts under cost constraints.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines
- PrivateLink across AWS accounts
- Multi-tenant isolation strategies (shared vs. per-tenant containers)
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function routeTenant(input, modelRegistry) {
  const tenant = input.tenantId;
  if (!allowedTenants.has(tenant)) {
    throw new Error('Unauthorized tenant');
  }
  const modelVersion = modelRegistry.getModelVersion(tenant, 'latest');
  return invokeSageMaker(modelVersion.endpoint, input);
}
```

